        <body>
            <div xml:id="d756">

                <pb facs="0614" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11849.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mediators.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellencies</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your note of May 5, by which you inform the Department that the
                    city of Niagara Falls, Canada, has been selected as the place for the
                    conferences of the mediators between the United States and Mexico, and that
                    their deliberations will commence there on May 18.</p>
                <p>The Department has duly noted your statement, in your note, that you have been
                    officially informed by the Administration of General Huerta that it will be
                    represented at the conference by Messrs. Emilio Rabasa, Augustín Rodríguez, and
                    Luis Elguero, and that Mr. Rafael Elguero will act as their secretary.</p>
                <p>Thanking you for the information conveyed, I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
